# Machine-local environment. Created once by chezmoi, then owned by you.
# Sourced from ~/.bashrc before the interactive guard, so `bash -lc` and the
# shell sshd starts for `ssh host cmd` see it as well as an interactive
# shell. A plain `bash -c` from a clean environment reads neither ~/.bashrc
# nor ~/.bash_profile, so nothing here reaches it. ~/.bashrc.local runs
# after the guard and is the place for aliases, functions, and anything
# else interactive-only.
#
# Exports and PATH only. Anything that writes to stdout breaks scp and
# other non-interactive callers.
#
# Extend PATH with `__path_prepend <dir>`, which ~/.bashrc keeps defined for
# this file. It skips a directory that is already on PATH or does not exist.
# A plain PATH="$dir:$PATH" doubles the entry every time a shell starts
# inside another one:
# __path_prepend "$HOME/.npm-global/bin"
#
# This is where a tool installer's edit belongs. rustup, for example,
# appends its line to ~/.bashrc and ~/.bash_profile, which chezmoi manages
# and rewrites on the next apply:
# [ -r "$HOME/.cargo/env" ] && . "$HOME/.cargo/env"
